{"agent":"pgreen","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"Moving the check dropped the `except Exception: return False` that wrapped `urlparse`. `urllib.parse.urlparse(\"http://[[REDACTED:ipv6]\")` (unclosed IPv6 brackets) raises `ValueError: Invalid IPv6 URL`. The only caller in `_eventlog.py` used to treat that as non-local and `continue`; it now raises and aborts the local-endpoint scan for any other blocks in the same config.","digest":"8393dc8bff0e8cee","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/http.py:local_endpoint","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/http.py:local_endpoint"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The bug names four recovery/brief tests plus a required regression test that fails on unfixed code. This diff only relocates `local_endpoint` and deletes `` `ddflow_diff` `` from an error string. None of `tests/test_brief_recovery_all.py` or `tests/test_recovery_plan.py` is touched, and no regression test is added, so those failures stay red and the promised `--regression-test` close-out cannot be satisfied by this change.","digest":"7bec3318a6cce024","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/handoff/send.py:71","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/handoff/send.py:71"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":0,"delta_from":"63f5ffab1b291af936fe6404adf5a57c3f35d288","delta_raised":[],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":706,"diff_sha":"fc62933382f7321d633cef466f1bb4605220758f3d9f8912a8dd8c58dc341689","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 63f5ffab1b","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":22.6,"family":"xai","findings":2,"full_coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"d6280d5ab5e0d349","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Be3461fc98e.critic.grok-4.7.20261109T235543Z-794796a0.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"e6